# Scalar
![](/images/Rscalar.png){style="width:100px; background: white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

Now to cover <u id='data_structure_tooltip'>__data structures__</u>, with the first being <u id='scalar_tooltip'>__scalars__</u>.

A <u id='scalar_tooltip'>__scalar__</u> consists of one value in an object. 
This can be one <u id='string_tooltip'>__string__</u>, one __numeric__, one <u id='logical_tooltip'>__logical__</u> etc. 

Create and run the below code to view a few <u id='scalar_tooltip'>__scalars__</u>.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
#A number
1
#A string
"How long is a string?"
#A logical
TRUE
```
:::


We have only been working with <u id='scalar_tooltip'>__scalars__</u> thus far but this is about to change. 


